    "message": "Guidelines list acute kidney injury as a TDF toxicity and recommend substituting TDF with ABC when GFR <60 mL/min. Patient's creatinine rose sharply from 0.9 to 2.4 with severe dehydration, suggesting prerenal AKI from gastroenteritis rather than TDF nephrotoxicity. Two family members share the same illness, supporting infectious gastroenteritis. Urinalysis shows no protein or glycosuria, which argues against TDF-induced Fanconi syndrome. Urea:creatinine ratio of 24:1 is consistent with prerenal dehydration. TDF can cause renal toxicity, but abrupt creatinine rise after 2 years on stable therapy with clear volume loss favours dehydration attribution. Guidelines advise substituting TDF for severe toxicity, but resuming ART with substitution when stable is also described.",
